00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:17.680
No, yeah, but once you're falling, you can't like will yourself a certain way.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:22.100
Like in Super Mario Bros., when you fall from any height, you can still control Mario's momentum.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:23.780
Not so in Super Pitfall.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:26.420
You are locked to a free fall, straight down.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.920
Like, put the controller down, have a bathroom break.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:30.740
You're going to be falling for a while.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.320
So real fast, I'll do the objective here.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:39.260
In Super Pitfall, you have to locate a diamond, your niece, and your pet quick claw,

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:41.240
who is a lion, as Sam mentioned earlier.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:45.420
And you do this through a vast set of cave, of one cave.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.920
I was going to say caves. Vast set of cave.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.580
Honestly, you know what the way these translations work out sometimes?

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:51.800
That might have been in the game.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:54.280
Yeah. You're given no map.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.100
You must explore the cave.

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:58.900
And there's zero guidance to find any of those things.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.320
So if you want to find the diamond, the niece, your pet quick claw,

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.000
the manual wasn't telling you anything.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.800
But the game isn't also telling you anything either.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:10.100
There's no character in the game who says, like, hey, I think your niece is this way.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.300
Or, like, a sign with your niece or something like that.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:14.440
Like, anything that would help you.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:17.660
You just have to kind of explore the cave and figure out where those things are.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:21.560
You're limited to jumping, climbing ladders, and shooting a gun.

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.480
One hit and you're dead.

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:26.800
Similar games we've played are Spelunker and Metroid.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.140
I think that's my objective setup.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:31.760
So now that everybody understands the game that we're talking about,

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.960
I'm sure they're picturing it vividly in their heads,

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.120
we can talk gameplay.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.400
Who wants to start? I'll start real quick.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:41.300
While you may be vividly imagining what the game is like,

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.080
it's very much not that.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.880
Because if you were thinking, like, okay, you go around,

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:50.300
you search for keys, and then they'll unlock doors.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.200
Like, yeah, there are keys and there are doors,

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.500
but you can't see the keys.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.740
And you really can't see the doors.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:00.400
And you also don't really see much of anything.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:07.500
Because everything that you're trying to find does not have a sprite until you jump and get it.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.540
Like, you won't even get it just walking around.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.140
They're hidden so poorly.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.760
Like, it's not even a fun experience, I think.

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.280
I feel like maybe some people did, but...

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.120
It's not because here's why also.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:22.240
Like, so you said with enemies just kind of pop in, right?

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.500
Like, all of a sudden a frog is like mid-jump,

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:26.300
even though you didn't see him a second ago.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:29.060
And then you just take one step back and he despawns, right?

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.240
It's like, oh, great job, programmers.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.720
Like, I'll just glitch my way through the cave that I'm clearly hallucinating.

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:40.400
Yeah. The thing that got me the most, I think, was the waterfalls.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.420
Because the waterfalls are really glitchy on their own.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.200
And I don't know if this happened with you guys.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:47.440
I know exactly what you're going to say.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.140
But the sprites were, like, jumping back and forth.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:52.120
And I couldn't time my way through because the sprites kept jumping.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.840
And I didn't know where the hitbox was.

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:54.860
It's designed so you have to time your way through.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:57.580
And then also it glitches in a way that you absolutely cannot.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:02.100
Yes. There's a certain part where I think, like, you're walking over a log

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:06.980
and two waterfall sprites just, like, perfectly sync up

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:10.560
over and over and over again on loop so that you can't get through anything.

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:14.260
And so in that situation, you have to kind of, like, leave that area

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:18.900
and come back and hope that the waterfall, like, sets itself properly.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:22.220
Yeah. And so, like, good job there, too.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:25.480
I think we can talk a lot about, like, the glitches and errors of this game, though.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.800
Because even just...

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.840
Even when it's performing...

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:31.460
Even when it's acting as it should, it performs terribly.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:34.920
Right. Nothing about this game's controls are satisfying.

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:37.300
Because even shooting your gun, right?

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:40.600
Like, you would expect, like, okay, I shoot the gun.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.000
The bullet comes out.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:43.460
There's the spider.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.120
And then it just goes right past the spider.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.860
It's like... Yeah. And then I realized, oh, no, that's just something that can never be killed.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.560
Yeah, you can kill spiders. You're supposed to...

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:54.140
I don't know if it works on spiders or not, but you're supposed to, like...

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:58.420
There's little dips that have, like, a small ladder or a small area you can, like, go in.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.680
And if you go in there, jump up a little bit and shoot.

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:03.240
The bullet will be at the right level to hit those lower things.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.020
Those situations are so rare.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.460
But at that point, you're better off just jumping over the edges.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:09.860
Yeah, really. They're also harmless.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:11.540
It's weird, because you can crouch.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.320
And I thought maybe that's why you would tell you to do that.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:19.400
What does that do? It doesn't do anything, because your hitbox, even when you're standing, doesn't affect your head.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:23.600
Yeah. Well, I guess there's, like, the bats that, like, fly in that little swoopy pattern.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:24.780
The hitbox is the same.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.380
Yeah? The hitbox is the same.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.560
Those bats really angered me.

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:34.200
So, I think, like, one thing, though, is, like, we're talking about frogs, we're talking about spiders, we're talking about bats.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.500
The cave's got a variety of enemies.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.100
The problem is that there's no way to handle these enemies.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.980
Yeah. The only thing you can do is shoot a frog in the face.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:42.980
If it's a net jump.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:44.660
On the scorpions, too.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.520
Those things got me. Yeah, and they charge at you, too.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:56.620
They run at you. Yeah, so they give you, like, a nice variety of enemies, but the problem is, is that the way that the game controls itself, you can't really handle any of these enemies properly.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:16.240
Maybe if they were, if it were less crowded, because it's a very crowded cave, and I sometimes will just have to avoid just going anywhere where there's any kind of resistance, because I just die so often, and you only get three tries, so you don't really want to risk it.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:22.020
Like, the design of the game actually punishes you for exploring in some ways.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:39.540
Yeah. Well, I think the biggest thing that punishes you for exploring at all, and, you know, to Pitfall's, like, you know, credit, this is one of the things that the original game had going for it, was, like, the traps and the, you know, like, avoid the alligators when their mouths are open, or, you know, like, don't fall into the pits, you know?

00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:41.580
Like, that makes sense. It kind of telegraphs that stuff to you.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:42.560
Right, it telegraphs that stuff to you.

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:53.940
In this game, it's filled with different kinds of traps, but none of them you're prepared for because they're a screen over that you fall into, or they're, as you're coming up to them, like, a new enemy is there.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:57.680
The ceiling will just spontaneously fall with no, like, when you're under it.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:13.300
Yeah, all of a sudden, a, you know, there's a part where the top of the ceiling of the cave kind of collapses onto you, and, like, cool idea, you know, I think, like, also that would kill anybody and should realistically block the path back the other way.

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:21.060
But if you want to do it in the game, I'm fine with that, but also it's just, it was never communicated to that point, so you're absolutely going to die the first time it happens.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:22.680
And is it only the one spot?

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:23.680
I feel like maybe I just, like, backtracked.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:27.540
I think there's more than one. I feel like it just happens at some spots, and there's no way of knowing what's going to happen.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.160
It's not really a puzzle, it's just, you're going to die.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:35.720
That's it. I don't think they're random, but I definitely think it happens, like, in multiple places throughout the game.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:39.580
I think the game exposes you to a lot early on in terms of exploration.

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:48.900
Like, you can go a bunch of different ways and experience a bunch of different things, but after a while, you've kind of seen the cave.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:53.820
Yeah. And now you're just kind of like, where is any of the things I need to find?

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:58.780
Right? Like, how did people do on finding the diamond, the niece, or the pet?

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:00.000
I found the diamond.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:02.280
That's it. I didn't find anything.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:11.720
Also, I just wanted to note that in the manual, even when you find Rhonda, it says that she's been turned to stone,

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.500
and so that you have to find a flask of medicine also.

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:16.920
So that's not even...

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.840
Yeah, but that's like, yeah, that's like the twist early on.

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:22.100
Yeah, but it tells you that first thing in the manual also.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:26.180
Right. But I guess, like, you know, it's the prologue of the game.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.120
Not that anybody would stick around for longer than the prologue.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.900
Yeah. I wouldn't recommend it.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.740
So we have issues with the jump.

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:35.080
We have issues with the gun.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:38.460
There's a lot of enemies, but they're too small to even hit with your gun.

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:41.240
We didn't even talk about the limited ammunition.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:44.520
So in your gun, you get, I think, 12 bullets?

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.880
20. 20? Who cares?

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:51.040
Yeah. That's how I, when I ran out of bullets, I was like, all right, I just won't shoot anymore.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.520
It hasn't done anything for me.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.840
They tried to make it like a use them carefully because these are precious and you're going

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:59.940
to need them. And it's like, I don't think I really need them.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:03.360
Like, I'll just, honestly, I'll just, with the frogs, I'll just go the other way.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:07.580
You know, like, honestly, in this cave, I'm thinking about how do I get back up to where

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:08.860
I came from and just leave?

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:10.740
Yeah. And it's not like the bullets work.

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:15.240
Also, I feel like the hitboxes were so bad on the enemies that I would have to shoot

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:17.620
the bat three times before we even get hit.

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:20.560
Yeah. And then you're down to 17 and good luck finding more ammo.

00:22:20.660 --> 00:22:21.740
There is more ammo, but.

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:25.160
It's hidden the same way that the keys are hidden, where you don't really see it until

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:27.240
you jump up and accidentally touch it.

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:30.600
Right. And that's even how the secret warps are dealt with in this game.

00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:33.000
Did we mention there's secret warps?

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:35.320
Yeah. There's secret warps to better manage your trip.

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:37.560
Secret, is that what they say in the mail?

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:42.640
I don't know. Okay. Secret warps in this game work a little differently, though, because sometimes secret warps are,

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:48.520
like, required to get back to other parts of the cave that you maybe fell from or that

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:49.520
you want to get back to.

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:51.900
That doesn't seem like that should be the case.

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:55.080
It should be that any way to get to this cave should be completely explorable.

00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:59.660
There should never be, like, a drop-off point unless it was going to act like a Metroidvania

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:04.780
where it's like, once you drop off, you can only get back to the top with the new item.

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:12.400
Yeah. You know? That level of design understanding is beyond the developer of this game.

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:19.000
Yes. One of the warps is actually an enemy that you have to get hit by.

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:20.720
And what's the problem with that, Sean?

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:27.240
The problem with that is that you have been trained from the beginning of this game to

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:29.700
either avoid or destroy enemies.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:34.160
I mean, it would take you forever to figure that out, even by accident.

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:37.740
Or, like, if you're intentionally doing it, you still don't know which enemy or anything.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:41.100
Surely the bird is colored differently or looks different.

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:43.960
The bird looks exactly like the other birds that can kill you, Mike.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:45.340
No way.

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:47.020
It is true.

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:50.600
And I only found this out by watching a video thing later on.

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:51.980
I can't believe that.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:58.160
That is the kind of stuff that when people say Nintendo hard, that's what I really think about.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:00.400
No, Nintendo game is designed that way.

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:04.360
Yeah, I know. But I'm saying, like, that's the kind of bullshit I expect from these kinds of games.

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:10.600
But this is the first, like, example I can think of where a game has, like, mandatory parts of it.

00:24:10.600 --> 00:24:15.720
Like, sometimes you will need to use that secret warp if you forgot something earlier on to get back to that area.

00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:19.100
And it's like, how would that be communicated to anybody?

00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:21.480
Were they trying to sell a guidebook later on?

00:24:21.720 --> 00:24:25.700
I don't know. That has to be something along those lines because I know that they did exist.

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:27.260
Like, there were strategy guides.

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:28.780
It's not even clever.

00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:37.420
No. Nowhere, you know, secret warps existing in an otherwise totally realistic world is, you know, mind-boggling enough.

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:41.980
But then to think, like, oh, and one of those secret worlds would just be a bird that you jump into.

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:44.460
It would be fun if that were, like, an Easter egg.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:46.080
Or maybe there was...

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:47.180
Takes you to a treasure room.

00:24:47.300 --> 00:24:48.620
Yeah. Something like that.

00:24:48.740 --> 00:24:52.140
But if it's actually necessary, then no.

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:57.020
No. There was a thing in The Goonies, too, that had that same thing, right?

00:24:57.040 --> 00:24:58.320
It was hit the woman five times.

00:24:58.760 --> 00:25:00.940
Oh, yeah. And then you get an evident required item.

00:25:00.940 --> 00:25:02.460
I don't know if it was a woman, but I think it was.

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:03.820
I think it was, like, an old woman. It was an old lady.

00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:05.700
Yeah, an old lady, and you got to hit her five times.

00:25:05.740 --> 00:25:12.660
All right, whatever. Whatever. And so, you know, we touched lightly on the exploration thing, I think, for the most part.

00:25:12.660 --> 00:25:13.580
I feel good about that.

00:25:13.660 --> 00:25:18.920
But can we talk about how there are no cave exploration items to be found in this game?

00:25:18.920 --> 00:25:24.520
I felt like a flashlight would have been nice, maybe some hiking gear, like, you know, a hookshot.

00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:25.660
Where were these things?

00:25:25.660 --> 00:25:26.600
So, all right.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:31.920
Do you, Mike, you know the trademark swinging ropes, right?

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:34.020
Yes. So those are from Pitfall.

00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:35.700
They're also in Pitfall 2.

00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:37.220
Super Pitfall, I'm sorry.

00:25:37.420 --> 00:25:42.120
Yeah. Well, this is a loose adaptation of Pitfall 2.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:46.140
Did you notice that they made, that they were sort of, like, phasing in and out of existence?

00:25:46.660 --> 00:25:49.640
Everything in this game, at one point or another, will phase in and out.

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:52.520
But no, I didn't notice this specific instance.

00:25:52.520 --> 00:26:11.800
I think that this, they pushed the engine, I mean, I don't even know if it's an engine that they built this game in, but they pushed the software so hard just to get the ropes to exist in some dimension that I don't think that there would be any processing power left to create, like, a hookshot.

00:26:12.200 --> 00:26:14.640
Let alone an inventory system, too.

00:26:14.920 --> 00:26:16.600
You know? Like, I don't think so.

00:26:16.820 --> 00:26:18.420
Yeah. But it's something that I would have liked.

00:26:19.100 --> 00:26:22.060
And then, what happens when you beat the game?

00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:26.660
Joe. Well, let me break it to you here.

00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:27.760
I didn't beat the game.

00:26:27.980 --> 00:26:29.280
Okay, that's fair. Do you know?

00:26:29.300 --> 00:26:34.720
I did watch the playthrough, and I saw that at the end, you get to, um, you get to, what, your niece that you're trying to rescue?

00:26:34.960 --> 00:26:38.420
Mm-hmm. You get her, and then that's, you're still playing the game.

00:26:38.720 --> 00:26:40.540
Yes. So you don't even get out, right?

00:26:41.020 --> 00:26:42.560
You have to go back somewhere.

00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:47.580
But, like, it didn't seem clearly indicated, even once you got there, why you've now, why it's over.

00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:49.580
I would imagine that you have to get out first.

00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:52.040
I don't know the exact clear conditions.

00:26:52.040 --> 00:27:01.920
I just know that when you clear, and we can find out the clear conditions in a minute, but once you clear the game, all you get is just offer to play in another world.

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:03.980
Oh, yeah. That's the actual ending.

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:13.260
Yeah. And it's just, this new world is just another game of Super Pitfall, but all of the items are switched to different locations.

00:27:13.460 --> 00:27:15.080
Which are already hidden. So, yeah.

00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:16.180
Like, no thanks.

00:27:16.540 --> 00:27:19.660
It was hard enough to find out in the first time without any indication of anything.

00:27:19.980 --> 00:27:25.040
This is the equivalent of, like, solving a puzzle, you know, like an actual jigsaw puzzle.

00:27:25.340 --> 00:27:29.460
And then after you solve it, they give you the option to solve the same puzzle.

00:27:29.580 --> 00:27:35.160
Like, you'll complete the same picture, but they change the shape of the jigsaws inside, you know?

00:27:35.380 --> 00:27:36.300
That's not helpful.

00:27:36.480 --> 00:27:41.920
That's not interesting. It's also not another realm or another dimension or whatever they said.

00:27:42.320 --> 00:27:45.100
Right. It's just things moved, things in different places.

00:27:46.040 --> 00:27:51.060
Let me give you the description of, like, how I watched the game end.

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:57.900
A lot of the things that I've learned about this game, I watched by, I learned by watching an AGDQ run.

00:27:58.580 --> 00:27:59.900
What is AGDQ?

00:28:00.240 --> 00:28:01.580
Awesome Games Done Quick.

00:28:01.580 --> 00:28:04.900
A little speedrunning marathon that's done two times a year.

00:28:05.040 --> 00:28:07.340
Yeah. He got awesome, and then he got Summer Games Done Quick.

00:28:07.500 --> 00:28:10.240
Very good. I don't know which one this was.

00:28:10.240 --> 00:28:11.180
I think it was awesome.

00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:14.140
But it did it in seven minutes.

00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:24.900
And the way he beat the game was he got his niece, and then he just died three times and ran out of his lives.

00:28:25.080 --> 00:28:28.720
And then he got to the title screen and waited for, like, the demo to run.

00:28:29.400 --> 00:28:34.520
And that pretty much works the same as whatever the other endgame, like, flag is supposed to be.

00:28:34.580 --> 00:28:44.200
Because the game is programmed so poorly that it thinks that the first frame of the demo, of the, like, attract mode, is you completing the game.

00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:47.360
And that's how the game ends, to me.

00:28:47.380 --> 00:28:51.280
I'm trying to even figure out how those are, like, accidentally connected.

00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:54.520
It's just poor, like, script programming.

00:28:56.460 --> 00:29:01.000
And so I'm watching it now, and it's kind of incredible.

00:29:01.200 --> 00:29:02.740
You do have to leave the cave.

00:29:02.960 --> 00:29:08.900
You find out that you've been in Egypt this whole time because every game takes place in Egypt at one point or another.

00:29:09.120 --> 00:29:12.380
One stage is going to casually reveal to you that there's pyramids in it.

00:29:12.380 --> 00:29:22.900
So you see the pyramids, and then the game just all of a sudden just starts, like, fluttering between, like, a black strobe and the actual gameplay.

00:29:23.020 --> 00:29:27.160
And then it just comes up and says, please try another world.

00:29:28.080 --> 00:29:30.100
That sounds like you've got the wrong number.

00:29:30.460 --> 00:29:34.500
Yeah. Like, you've been playing the wrong game, and they tell you once you've finished it.

00:29:34.600 --> 00:29:35.980
Like, oh, wait, this wasn't the game.

00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:37.860
That was somebody else's niece.

00:29:38.980 --> 00:29:40.880
You have to go back and find your niece.

00:29:41.140 --> 00:29:42.660
You don't recognize your own niece?

00:29:42.980 --> 00:29:45.880
That was also, like, a gumshoe problem, right?

00:29:46.380 --> 00:29:47.820
Later that same day.

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:49.780
Yeah, later that same day, she's kidnapped.

00:29:50.960 --> 00:29:52.000
That was a good game.

00:29:52.480 --> 00:30:25.040
Not. Let's, um, let's fix this mess.

00:30:25.520 --> 00:30:27.960
Would you guys join me in fixing this mess?

00:30:28.180 --> 00:30:34.760
Let's think about what we would want in this game to make Super Pitfall a game that you would actually play.

00:30:34.760 --> 00:30:44.640
Because I think this is a game that is so bad in terms of how it actually controls and in terms of, like, what they chose to include.

00:30:44.800 --> 00:30:50.500
That if we think about what is possible in the realm of the NES, I think I can do this.

00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:51.700
I thought this one through.

00:30:51.980 --> 00:30:53.360
And so here's what I have, okay?

00:30:54.120 --> 00:30:58.240
No traps that you can't see on screen beforehand.

00:30:58.240 --> 00:31:04.400
So there's, like, a warning or a cue that something's going to fall apart or that.

00:31:04.720 --> 00:31:06.480
A rumble. Yeah, a rumble or something.

00:31:06.680 --> 00:31:09.520
Or that, like, a ladder leads to, like, a pit.

00:31:09.640 --> 00:31:14.280
You know, so you can at least go down there and then be like, I don't really want to fall into that and climb back up.

00:31:14.740 --> 00:31:20.720
Things that don't necessarily, like, auto-kill you for a mistake that you wouldn't have made had you have known more information.

00:31:20.720 --> 00:31:26.180
Because if you think about it, if you're exploring a cave, there's nothing stopping a guy on a ladder from looking down and saying,

00:31:26.280 --> 00:31:28.180
oh, that's a pit, and then going back up.

00:31:28.480 --> 00:31:29.880
Because we the player can't see that.

00:31:29.940 --> 00:31:31.540
I don't think it's fair that our character dies.

00:31:32.600 --> 00:31:35.500
Next, I don't think there should be a giant map.

00:31:35.640 --> 00:31:41.840
But I think that there should have been maps found throughout the game that lead you to the next area you need to go to.

00:31:41.840 --> 00:31:50.340
So there's a clear sense of direction that, you know, okay, cool, I've completed, you know, like, the upper right portion of the screen,

00:31:50.340 --> 00:31:55.460
and now I need to move down, you know, like, just kind of like, here's where you've been, here's where you need to go next.

00:31:55.880 --> 00:31:56.720
Something like that.

00:31:57.820 --> 00:32:03.800
I would have also liked an above-ground area that you need to deliver things found in the cave.

00:32:04.040 --> 00:32:07.400
So, obviously, there would be more here than just your niece, the diamond, and...

00:32:07.400 --> 00:32:09.280
You want to introduce more backtracking?

00:32:09.480 --> 00:32:11.660
And the pet. But, yeah, well, here's the reason why.

00:32:11.840 --> 00:32:19.060
It would have made me become more familiar with the layout of the cave, rather than thinking, like, that the cave is just...

00:32:19.060 --> 00:32:20.720
I don't know where I am compared to where I'm going.

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:26.800
You'd have to learn the routes between, like, if there's something in the top right of the game, you'd have to figure out,

00:32:26.860 --> 00:32:31.940
okay, now how do I get back to the main starting point to deliver and drop off these things?

00:32:31.980 --> 00:32:39.080
I'm not saying there would be, like, a marketplace where you actually, like, barter and sell things, but just almost like...

00:32:39.080 --> 00:32:40.660
A home base. Yeah, a home base.

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:44.640
You know what's funny? What you're describing sounds so much like SteamWorld Dig.

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:46.060
Yeah, this is SteamWorld Dig right now.

00:32:46.080 --> 00:32:47.000
Have you played that game?

00:32:47.060 --> 00:32:48.360
I've played SteamWorld Dig, yes.

00:32:48.680 --> 00:32:50.000
But they have marketplaces.

00:32:50.140 --> 00:32:51.180
That's funny. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:32:51.300 --> 00:32:52.380
Okay, no. No marketplace.

00:32:52.700 --> 00:32:57.140
Just, like... I'm thinking more like the Game & Watch octopus game.

00:32:57.340 --> 00:33:00.720
Yeah. Where, like, Mario goes down and he can loot the treasure.

00:33:01.100 --> 00:33:01.920
It's not Mario.

00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:02.940
It's Game & Watch in that one.

00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:05.300
But I'm thinking of the Game & Watch gallery for Game Boy.

00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:10.740
But you loot the treasure for as much as you'd like, but then your character gets heavier and smaller as you come back up.

00:33:10.920 --> 00:33:13.600
And then you just drop off all the coins that you've collected.

00:33:13.960 --> 00:33:17.860
Otherwise, if you get caught by the octopus, you lose everything.

00:33:17.860 --> 00:33:18.960
So what are your other...

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:20.120
Do you have any more, like, big points?

00:33:20.320 --> 00:33:25.260
The other thing I was thinking was more booby traps, not cheap deaths.

00:33:25.520 --> 00:33:29.380
Think more, like, Indiana Jones-style booby traps in the cave.

00:33:29.840 --> 00:33:32.380
They can shamelessly take, like, a rolling rock.

00:33:32.520 --> 00:33:33.700
I would have liked that.

00:33:33.740 --> 00:33:35.520
That exists in sort of a...

00:33:36.160 --> 00:33:37.260
The Moai Head.

00:33:37.600 --> 00:33:38.660
Yes. Which is in every game.

00:33:39.920 --> 00:33:41.380
We need to talk about the Moai Head.

00:33:41.480 --> 00:33:43.240
Every game should have a Moai Head, like, section.

00:33:43.240 --> 00:33:44.480
I didn't want to talk about the Moai Head.

00:33:44.580 --> 00:33:45.460
It scared you?

00:33:45.460 --> 00:33:46.620
I'm scared of the Moai Head now.

00:33:46.740 --> 00:33:50.140
Well, this one is rather, like, large and...

00:33:50.140 --> 00:33:53.260
Imposing. Imposing compared to the other Moai Heads we've faced.

00:33:53.740 --> 00:34:01.220
But other than the Moai Head, they also have, you know, the stereotypical action movie Vice Room,

00:34:01.260 --> 00:34:03.520
where things just sort of try and crush you.

00:34:03.700 --> 00:34:05.720
Yes, which is also in, like, Castlevania.

00:34:05.940 --> 00:34:07.960
Yeah. So, I mean, they do exist.

00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:09.960
They're just not very well executed.

00:34:11.060 --> 00:34:15.160
Which is, yeah, just down to, again, the poor programming of everything in the game.

00:34:15.460 --> 00:34:26.020
I do think, though, that with your changes, you would also have to change several different core concepts that govern a lot of these early NES games.

00:34:26.020 --> 00:34:32.260
Like the idea of one-hit deaths and limited lives.

00:34:32.260 --> 00:34:34.300
Because if you're going to be doing...

00:34:34.300 --> 00:34:44.220
I feel like the mode of exploration that the designers, in quotes, of this game were expecting you to do was,

00:34:44.340 --> 00:34:49.180
you learn the beginning by dying over and over, and you have to go through it over and over.

00:34:49.180 --> 00:34:55.160
When you introduce, well, you have to go back anyway to deliver your goods.

00:34:55.420 --> 00:35:02.100
I think that if you have both the limited amount of lives and the, I guess, like, restart,

00:35:03.420 --> 00:35:06.220
the amount of times that you have to restart and start from the beginning anyway,

00:35:06.500 --> 00:35:10.020
I think that adding more backtracking will be annoying.

00:35:10.020 --> 00:35:16.480
But if you have, like, maybe a health bar and unlimited continues, then maybe, yeah, that would work.

00:35:16.760 --> 00:35:23.940
To be fair, I completely stand by that every NES game should lose lives and have a health bar instead of a one-hit death.

00:35:24.080 --> 00:35:29.760
However, in this game, I'm cool with a one-hit death because, like, you're just some random dude just down in a cave.

00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:31.160
Scorpion stings you.

00:35:31.340 --> 00:35:32.960
You're dead. Is there still a gun?

00:35:33.600 --> 00:35:34.860
There's still a gun, yes.

00:35:34.860 --> 00:35:37.980
And it works. It kills all enemies in my version of the game.

00:35:37.980 --> 00:35:43.300
I think that there's a precedent for a health bar, though, because in the very first pitfall, that's how,

00:35:43.380 --> 00:35:45.300
it's not a health bar, but it's, like, a health number.

00:35:45.540 --> 00:35:47.540
Yeah, yeah, you get, like, three, I think.

00:35:48.340 --> 00:35:50.000
Three? Before you're, like...

00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:54.120
They're basically lives. Right, but when you, like, hit the ground too hard, your number goes down as well.

00:35:54.180 --> 00:35:56.440
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, I didn't even connect that.

00:35:56.660 --> 00:35:58.280
Yeah. I didn't really know what it did.

00:35:58.280 --> 00:35:59.320
I thought it was just my score.

00:35:59.780 --> 00:36:00.960
Oh, I assumed that was health.

00:36:01.080 --> 00:36:02.000
Maybe I was wrong. Yeah.

00:36:02.260 --> 00:36:06.220
But, I don't know, I think a health bar, I agree.

00:36:06.580 --> 00:36:07.500
Yeah. That's what I gotta say.

00:36:07.980 --> 00:36:11.700
I agree. Yeah, no, I would like a health bar in every NES game, and as you guys know, sometimes

00:36:11.700 --> 00:36:15.460
I try to, like, track down ROM hacks that have fixed this in games.

00:36:16.500 --> 00:36:25.720
And, lo and behold, there is a super pitfall ROM hack that goes above and beyond any ROM hack

00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:27.520
I've seen for an NES game so far.

00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:28.860
Is this the one that was just released?

00:36:29.100 --> 00:36:30.880
It was released pretty recently.

00:36:30.880 --> 00:36:32.960
Let me check the date for you on this.

00:36:32.960 --> 00:36:34.840
Because it's also, like, a remastered version, right?

00:36:34.840 --> 00:36:38.760
No, this is September 5th, 2016.

00:36:39.220 --> 00:36:42.220
Okay. But, this is the remastered version.

00:36:42.260 --> 00:36:44.360
It does work on a regular NES.

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:50.900
If you have, like, a flash cartridge that can work on a regular NES and you plug with this

00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:53.440
ROM hack in, it will play properly on original hardware.

00:36:53.780 --> 00:36:58.760
The crazy thing is, it redesigns almost everything about this game.

00:36:58.760 --> 00:37:01.360
It's called Super Pitfall 30th Anniversary Edition.

00:37:01.420 --> 00:37:04.700
This is what I'm talking about. And it's by, it's a hack by NES Rocks.

00:37:05.160 --> 00:37:10.460
I thought he would be known for more because this is such an amazing ROM hack, but he's

00:37:10.460 --> 00:37:12.400
just known as the Super Pitfall guy.

00:37:12.420 --> 00:37:13.940
It looks pretty great, too. I played it.

00:37:14.220 --> 00:37:15.720
And it is fantastic.

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:22.280
It's got completely new graphics, a new soundtrack, a new menu that's more colorful and plays,

00:37:22.500 --> 00:37:26.560
you know, like, looks more like Pitfall and shows the pyramids right off the bat so

00:37:26.560 --> 00:37:28.500
there's no, like, confusion about that.

00:37:29.400 --> 00:37:33.420
When they say that there's improved performance, they mean it because even the jump is fixed

00:37:33.420 --> 00:37:37.320
and you can move while you're falling down mid-momentum.

00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:45.080
That's cute. The only thing that was kind of weird with Super Pitfall was that the gun, even though it

00:37:45.080 --> 00:37:48.680
still exists and stuff like that, it doesn't always seem to trigger when you want it to.

00:37:49.020 --> 00:37:50.380
So that was maybe just like a...

00:37:50.380 --> 00:37:52.280
That's just keeping with the Super Pitfall heritage, though.

00:37:52.440 --> 00:37:55.200
Yeah, yeah. But there's no more hidden items.

00:37:55.200 --> 00:37:59.220
Warps are now doors instead of just, like, things you run into.

00:38:00.420 --> 00:38:03.940
There's a new HUD inside the game that explains more things to you.

00:38:04.740 --> 00:38:09.320
There are little, like, level design adjustments to make sure that the very first ladder doesn't

00:38:09.320 --> 00:38:11.200
lead to a pit of death.

00:38:11.500 --> 00:38:12.760
Like, that's nice.

00:38:13.260 --> 00:38:15.620
And if you can believe it, it's also...

00:38:16.760 --> 00:38:19.060
It's available in English and Portuguese.

00:38:19.640 --> 00:38:21.200
So it's not even just a one...

00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:23.640
I've always been looking for that Portuguese experience.

00:38:23.980 --> 00:38:30.580
Right, right. And the last thing, a seamless, fully automatic save feature.

00:38:30.900 --> 00:38:37.180
You just hold reset while shutting down and it will avoid save file corruption.

00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:38.820
That's fun. Wow.

00:38:39.060 --> 00:38:41.060
Good job, NES Rocks.

00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:43.040
Crazy. I love it.

00:38:43.920 --> 00:38:50.920
I also hope, because I need to go back to more bugs, that they fixed this particular issue.

00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:56.460
I think they found a bug, decided they didn't want to fix it, and then just made it canon.

00:38:57.360 --> 00:38:59.060
But there is...

00:38:59.060 --> 00:39:01.960
You notice that you'll just fall off ladders, right?

00:39:02.520 --> 00:39:03.680
Yeah, I've noticed.

00:39:03.860 --> 00:39:05.660
I don't think that that was designed.

00:39:05.780 --> 00:39:08.720
I think that that was a problem that they did not fix.

00:39:08.860 --> 00:39:10.040
But it is in the manual.

00:39:10.040 --> 00:39:13.480
It is in the manual. So maybe they retroactively were like, let's just make it look like we planned it.

00:39:13.480 --> 00:39:14.500
So they have to fix that.

00:39:14.640 --> 00:39:16.980
But also, if there are...

00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:19.600
This is another thing that I learned from the speedrun.

00:39:19.980 --> 00:39:27.240
If you are in a screen where there are any moving sprites at all, whether it's an enemy

00:39:27.240 --> 00:39:33.160
or a moving platform or something in the background, you can just phase through walls if you walk

00:39:33.160 --> 00:39:34.700
in that direction for long enough.

00:39:35.420 --> 00:39:41.820
And it's just all these bugs means that this game wasn't even playtested, I feel like.

00:39:41.960 --> 00:39:47.060
But Super Pitfall 30th Anniversary Edition proves that this is all possible.

00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:48.820
Like, remember when you were talking earlier about the...

00:39:48.820 --> 00:39:52.480
I didn't want to spoil it, but when you were talking about the ropes and how they were kind

00:39:52.480 --> 00:39:55.040
of like glitching in and out, that's just like...

00:39:55.040 --> 00:39:57.500
That's just because they didn't know how to code this game properly.

00:39:57.900 --> 00:40:02.960
Exactly, yeah. You know, granted, this is in 2016 where we know a lot more about programming, but one

00:40:02.960 --> 00:40:07.460
guy was able to completely fix this game and make it into something that's, at least for

00:40:07.460 --> 00:40:09.480
Pitfall fans, something more faithful.

00:40:09.680 --> 00:40:14.340
I'm not saying that anybody who likes NES games should try this, but I definitely think this

00:40:14.340 --> 00:40:18.020
is more true to the Pitfall franchise than Super Pitfall ever was.

00:40:18.180 --> 00:40:23.820
Yeah. And it's not like by 1987 there hadn't been other games that were at least as big as Pitfall

00:40:23.820 --> 00:40:24.640
that did better.

00:40:24.760 --> 00:40:27.840
Yeah. So it's not like, you know, it's not like they're like, ah, we gotta give them a break

00:40:27.840 --> 00:40:30.200
because they, you know, no one knew how to do this yet.

00:40:30.360 --> 00:40:31.280
Like, it's... Oh, yeah.

00:40:31.480 --> 00:40:33.140
No, I didn't give them a break of any kind.

00:40:33.140 --> 00:40:34.860
I just imagined that...

00:40:34.860 --> 00:40:36.860
When I said engine, I thought I...

00:40:36.860 --> 00:40:38.580
I meant sort of like a...

00:40:38.580 --> 00:40:40.180
This is beyond their capability.

00:40:40.320 --> 00:40:41.860
Oh, right. Capability. Yes, completely.

00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:45.780
And while we're on the subject of the ROM hacks, I just also wanted to talk about,

00:40:45.860 --> 00:40:50.480
because we didn't talk about this in the Goonies 2 episode, but NES Rocks, that same

00:40:50.480 --> 00:40:54.260
guy, also made a Goonies 2 redesign, which...

00:40:54.260 --> 00:40:56.180
Cleaning up the entire...

00:40:56.780 --> 00:40:57.660
Yeah. All the bad ones.

00:40:57.780 --> 00:40:59.940
Yeah, that one I'd be pretty interested to play, because I liked Goonies 2.

00:41:00.040 --> 00:41:02.200
Yeah. Already. I mean, it had a lot of problems, but...

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:03.420
So I'll just tell you a few things.

00:41:03.560 --> 00:41:05.080
The text is now faster.

00:41:05.820 --> 00:41:10.160
Pressing the select button toggles between hyper and jump shoes, if you have any of those.

00:41:10.160 --> 00:41:11.720
This is Goonies 2. Yeah, Goonies 2.

00:41:12.360 --> 00:41:17.200
The start button goes to the map screen, and pausing has been removed, because obviously,

00:41:17.400 --> 00:41:19.520
like, you're paused on the map screen anyway.

00:41:20.140 --> 00:41:24.540
There's a better password screen with more information on controls, and also way more intuitive

00:41:24.540 --> 00:41:29.960
controls. There's a new map screen showing the location of some important items right off the bat,

00:41:30.020 --> 00:41:32.460
so this way you don't have to just look around for things.

00:41:32.980 --> 00:41:36.580
You know, some people say it's not necessary, but I think in today's day and age, it's important

00:41:36.580 --> 00:41:40.820
to have, like, something to start from, not to just start from the bare minimum.

00:41:41.700 --> 00:41:45.200
And you only need to hit the lady once instead of five times.

00:41:45.580 --> 00:41:46.740
So that's a big improvement.

00:41:46.740 --> 00:41:51.320
It's much nicer. It's still not great, but it's a little nicer than five times.

00:41:51.520 --> 00:42:00.560
A review in Computer Gaming World, this is in 1987, hated Super Pitfall and said that

00:42:00.560 --> 00:42:02.660
it was a Super Mario Bros.

00:42:03.080 --> 00:42:06.440
rehash that most NES users will be able to play.

00:42:06.580 --> 00:42:07.540
in their sleep.

00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:11.580
Certainly, there is nothing in the game itself to keep them awake.

00:42:11.820 --> 00:42:13.680
I could agree with the second sentence.

00:42:13.920 --> 00:42:16.840
I have no idea how this is like Super Mario Bros.

00:42:17.120 --> 00:42:21.540
I am Jump. And he looks like Super Mario.

00:42:21.780 --> 00:42:23.100
This is a lazy review.

00:42:23.380 --> 00:42:26.560
The color scheme kind of looks like the bricks.

00:42:26.980 --> 00:42:27.980
Yeah, the bricks, I guess.

