You know who he reminds me of?

00:42:32.720 --> 00:42:34.240
He reminds me of Blue Luigi.

00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:35.540
Blue Luigi.

00:42:35.540 --> 00:42:37.520
The alternate costume in Smash Bros?

00:42:37.820 --> 00:42:38.780
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'm like, ah.

00:42:38.900 --> 00:42:41.920
I'm still wondering, though, why they thought this game was so easy.

00:42:42.280 --> 00:42:44.200
Yeah. Yeah, that's what I was confused, too.

00:42:44.260 --> 00:42:45.380
People could play it in their sleep.

00:42:45.560 --> 00:42:47.240
I mean, I think it's difficult.

00:42:47.580 --> 00:42:49.280
I think it will put you to sleep.

00:42:49.280 --> 00:42:53.200
I don't think this is a game people today would say.

00:42:53.200 --> 00:43:01.300
We've had the same sort of questioning the reviewer of the past where they think something is so easy and it's actually very hard.

00:43:01.460 --> 00:43:03.980
But maybe that's just our modern sensibilities getting in the way.

00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:14.320
Yeah, maybe it's not that it's particularly difficult to avoid enemies, but it's just difficult to get your objectives done and play this game in general.

00:43:14.920 --> 00:43:17.000
Yeah. I mean, it's also not that easy.

00:43:17.200 --> 00:43:19.500
It's not crazy easy to avoid enemies either.

00:43:19.760 --> 00:43:27.360
Yeah. So this is where Pitfall ends on the NES.

00:43:27.360 --> 00:43:28.880
We will not be playing another one.

00:43:29.120 --> 00:43:36.940
No. But I just wanted to talk about the sequels and spinoffs section for Super Pitfall and Pitfall in general.

00:43:37.520 --> 00:43:43.140
A sequel titled Super Pitfall 2 was planned, but then was canceled a short time later.

00:43:43.640 --> 00:43:45.820
I think it was probably because of sales.

00:43:46.220 --> 00:43:56.040
Yeah. It was going to be a localized version of Sunsoft's Famicom title Atlantis Nonazo, but I don't think that would help.

00:43:56.840 --> 00:44:00.400
Just stealing another game and then saying it's Super Pitfall 2.

00:44:00.660 --> 00:44:04.220
If anything, it would confuse fans of Super Pitfall, of which there were none.

00:44:06.500 --> 00:44:12.000
Then we get Pitfall the Mayan Adventure on Super Nintendo in 1994.

00:44:12.400 --> 00:44:13.580
People like this game though, right?

00:44:13.580 --> 00:44:16.640
People like this game and it also plays a lot more like Prince of Persia.

00:44:16.880 --> 00:44:20.300
Okay. So I think that's why at this time Prince of Persia is now a big deal.

00:44:20.420 --> 00:44:24.000
Prince of Persia came to Super Nintendo as well as it got ported to everything.

00:44:24.300 --> 00:44:28.320
Yeah. So I think now that was more like, oh, Prince of Persia, Pitfall, they go hand in hand.

00:44:28.420 --> 00:44:32.660
Let's make a Pitfall that's more like Prince of Persia.

00:44:33.240 --> 00:44:39.780
Then you get Pitfall 3D Beyond the Jungle for PlayStation and emphasis on 3D here.

00:44:39.880 --> 00:44:41.280
Please tell me it's like Tomb Raider.

00:44:41.900 --> 00:44:46.200
You know, I should tell you what it's like, but I wanted to say emphasis on 3D here because

00:44:46.200 --> 00:44:48.200
it's also on the Game Boy Color.

00:44:48.440 --> 00:44:49.400
Oh. Okay?

00:44:49.660 --> 00:44:51.180
And I'm confused.

00:44:52.200 --> 00:44:53.700
I don't really know what that means.

00:44:54.100 --> 00:44:59.960
Yeah. So just like in Pitfall the Mayan Adventure and the original Pitfall for the Atari 2600,

00:45:01.280 --> 00:45:04.420
the Mayan Adventure is a game set.

00:45:04.620 --> 00:45:06.620
Oh, no. It says just as in its...

00:45:06.620 --> 00:45:10.240
I don't know what this is trying to tell me right now, but it's trying to tell me that

00:45:10.240 --> 00:45:16.820
the original Pitfall for the Atari 2600 is available as an Easter egg for Pitfall the

00:45:16.820 --> 00:45:21.700
Mayan Adventure. Why that would be the first thing mentioned in the gameplay section of anybody's notes?

00:45:21.940 --> 00:45:23.280
Just the Wikipedia? Yeah.

00:45:23.400 --> 00:45:28.540
The official Wikipedia article lists what's included as an Easter egg before it ever talks

00:45:28.540 --> 00:45:29.580
about what the game is about.

00:45:29.720 --> 00:45:30.920
It must not be that good then.

00:45:31.040 --> 00:45:34.880
The Mayan Adventure is a game set in a 3D environment which allows the player character

00:45:34.880 --> 00:45:36.300
to move in any direction.

00:45:36.540 --> 00:45:37.980
Wow. Nobody played this game.

00:45:38.460 --> 00:45:43.540
The player character also has a much wider range of attacks, some of which must be acquired

00:45:43.540 --> 00:45:44.680
through item pickups.

00:45:44.980 --> 00:45:46.780
Finally, item pickups are a thing.

00:45:46.780 --> 00:45:49.200
Is there cover-based shooting?

00:45:50.480 --> 00:45:51.280
There is not.

00:45:51.460 --> 00:45:54.600
That was invented in Gears of War, right?

00:45:54.860 --> 00:45:56.240
There's cover-based shooting in this game.

00:45:56.320 --> 00:45:58.440
You jump into those pits and you jump up and you shoot.

00:45:58.440 --> 00:45:59.460
Oh, you shoot the spiders. Right.

00:46:00.400 --> 00:46:02.160
First instance of cover-based shooting.

00:46:02.320 --> 00:46:06.020
I wish we could capture how annoyed Sean looked.

00:46:06.180 --> 00:46:07.740
Sean looked alarmed.

00:46:07.800 --> 00:46:10.400
He was looking around like confused.

00:46:10.760 --> 00:46:15.440
I just know that cover-based shooting was not invented by the Gears of War people.

00:46:15.760 --> 00:46:17.500
I just know that. Oh, you were annoyed at that.

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:19.120
Yeah. I thought you were annoyed at the...

00:46:19.120 --> 00:46:21.100
No. The real people who invented it.

00:46:21.200 --> 00:46:24.920
But since I can't give you much about the gameplay, I will tell you that the plot to

00:46:24.920 --> 00:46:27.540
Pitfall 3D is that Pitfall Harry Jr.

00:46:28.560 --> 00:46:32.460
meets a girl named Myra who enlists his aid in freeing

00:46:32.460 --> 00:46:35.300
her people from the Scourge.

00:46:35.880 --> 00:46:42.740
The Scourge? Who sounds like a tribe maybe or like an alien entity.

00:46:43.120 --> 00:46:43.960
Yeah. Maybe a Scourge.

00:46:43.960 --> 00:46:47.980
It refers to just one evil woman bent on controlling the world.

00:46:48.260 --> 00:46:49.140
Oh, okay. Huh.

00:46:49.580 --> 00:46:51.820
So it's a little bit of like a step up in the stakes.

00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:53.640
Yeah. And I'm getting...

00:46:53.640 --> 00:46:59.680
It's set in a magical parallel universe where there are no...

00:47:01.620 --> 00:47:02.700
No, this is all garbage.

00:47:02.840 --> 00:47:06.180
They were like, if you think about Crash Bandicoot, this is like such...

00:47:06.640 --> 00:47:09.180
What? This is just a million out of thoughts.

00:47:09.180 --> 00:47:10.380
I mean, it's just like a fan just wrote this.

00:47:10.560 --> 00:47:15.680
Right. Somebody just went on like a rant one night and said, oh, if you think about Crash Bandicoot,

00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:18.560
this is way less linear.

00:47:18.680 --> 00:47:23.280
It wasn't even meant as the Pitfall Wikipedia page.

00:47:23.320 --> 00:47:26.420
They just wrote something and like, maybe I could tie this in and include it in the Pitfall

00:47:26.420 --> 00:47:31.940
Wikipedia page. So the last game we get is Pitfall The Lost Expedition.

00:47:32.160 --> 00:47:34.320
It's for the sixth generation consoles.

00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:37.400
It's GameCube, PS2, and Xbox.

00:47:37.940 --> 00:47:41.700
I don't want to even look at what the gameplay is for this kind of game, but I imagine that

00:47:41.700 --> 00:47:47.320
like... My opinion is that GameCube and PS2 and that stuff is where things kind of got okay, but

00:47:47.320 --> 00:47:49.700
I'm kind of done with that gen of things.

